<%# An invitation to write back, in the follow-up letter.

    Two independent questions here. Who is speaking (TheaterInfo#first_person?)
    decides the pronouns, as it does everywhere else in this mailer. Where the
    reply should go is separate: only a house with BOTH a named director and an
    address for them can say "email me", so anyone else sends patrons to the
    box office. With neither address configured there is no invitation worth
    extending, so nothing prints. %>
<% personal = theater_info.first_person? %>
<% reply_to_director = theater_info.artistic_director? %>
<% recipient = reply_to_director ? theater_info.artistic_director_email : theater_info.box_office_email %>
<% if recipient.present? %>
  <table class="w410" width="410" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0">
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td class="w410" width="410">
          <h5 align="left" class="article-title">
            Tell us about it
          </h5>
          <div align="left" class="article-content">
            <p>
              <% if personal %>
                I always want to hear from you about your experience in our home here at <%= theater_info.name %>.
              <% else %>
                We always want to hear about your experience at <%= theater_info.name %>.
              <% end %>
              <% if reply_to_director %>
                I hope you will feel free to email me at any time
                (<a href="mailto:<%= recipient %>"><%= recipient %></a>) to tell me about it.
              <% else %>
                Please feel free to email us at any time
                (<a href="mailto:<%= recipient %>"><%= recipient %></a>) to tell us about it.
              <% end %>
            </p>
          </div>
        </td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
<% end %>
